WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.549
A racy conversation between Tormund and Brienne,
Cersei in a blood-soaked bed, and Jon's farewell

00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:10.590
to Ghost were all chopped from season seven
of Game of Thrones.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.949
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm looking at some of the best

00:00:13.949 --> 00:00:19.070
scenes that ended up cut from the seventh
season of HBO's mega-popular fantasy series.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:23.630
By the way, my Game of Thrones Funko Pop giveaway
is also running on this video, so for a chance

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:27.189
to win: make sure you're subscribed to my
channel and leave a comment with your thoughts

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:29.859
about the deleted scenes or the show.

00:00:29.859 --> 00:00:35.590
And quick warning: I'm talking spoilers for
all seasons and speculation for season 8.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:39.510
The fearsome wildling leader Tormund Giantsbane
is one of my favourite characters on the show

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.430
and he's had some fantastic moments that bring
a lot of humour to the series.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:48.040
And ever since season six, when he first laid
eyes on the mighty warrior Brienne of Tarth,

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.080
the formidable Tormund has been struck down
with puppy love.

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:55.350
There have been some hilarious scenes of Tormund
eyeing up Brienne and so far she's ignored

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:59.230
his advances, but fans of the pair may be
sad to know that some lines of rather racy

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:03.500
dialogue between the two were cut from this
season's very first episode.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.520
The lost moment took place after Tormund approached
Brienne in Winterfell as she was sparring

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.609
with Podrick.

00:01:08.609 --> 00:01:12.999
The red-haired wildling was going to try flirting
with Brienne by telling her about his experience

00:01:12.999 --> 00:01:14.450
with Sheila the Bear.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:19.350
You can see a little clip still in the episode
where Brienne walks off in disgust while Sansa

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.350
and Littlefinger are talking overhead.

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:21.350
Sadly, though, Tormund and Brienne's actual
conversation was cut.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:24.649
This would have been a funny call-back to
season four when Tormund tried to impress

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:29.520
his fellow wildlings with his story claiming
he'd had carnal relations with a bear.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.439
"Oh that was a night to remember."

00:01:31.439 --> 00:01:39.630
"Her fangs were sharp, but she knew how to
use them."

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:40.894
"And she was nice and soft down beIow."

00:01:40.894 --> 00:01:41.979
"No, she was no ordinary beast."

00:01:41.979 --> 00:01:47.389
Ygritte was having none of Tormund's tall
tale back then and, clearly, Brienne wasn't

00:01:47.389 --> 00:01:52.159
impressed by it either, or as the actor who
plays Tormund says, "she didn't like [his]

00:01:52.159 --> 00:01:56.320
pick-up line" – which is hardly surprising
for all sorts of reasons including her own

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:00.220
experience having to fight a bear when she
was captured by Bolton men back in season

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.220
3.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:05.780
In fact, Brienne's pretty uncomfortable with
the whole Tormund situation, which was made

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:11.129
clear in a deleted scene from season 6 that
showed Sansa teasing her about Tormund's interest

00:02:11.129 --> 00:02:14.209
which sent the great warrior into a fluster
of embarrassment.

00:02:14.209 --> 00:02:19.500
Still, I do hope Tormund and Brienne survive
at least a good few episodes next season so

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.140
we can see their paths cross again.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:25.990
By the way, Tormund's attempted flirtation
with Brienne at Winterfell wasn't the only

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:30.330
moment featuring the wildling talking about
bears that ended up cut this season.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:34.910
In episode 6, when a giant undead polar bear
appeared out of nowhere to attack Jon Snow's

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:40.340
ranging party, the first words out of Tormund's
mouth were, 'I've danced with plenty of bears',

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:44.159
though that line sadly hit the editing room
floor.

00:02:44.159 --> 00:02:49.659
And the premiere episode also cut down another
scene, this time with Sam and Gilly.

00:02:49.659 --> 00:02:53.379
It's during the scene where Sam is studying
books from the Citadel's restricted library

00:02:53.379 --> 00:02:57.319
and remembers about the mountain of dragonglass
sitting beneath Dragonstone.

00:02:57.319 --> 00:03:01.519
In that scene, Gilly picked up a book called
"Legends of the Long Night" and started to

00:03:01.519 --> 00:03:02.519
read.

00:03:02.519 --> 00:03:06.310
Unfortunately, the part where Gilly reads
aloud from the book was reportedly cut out,

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:11.469
so we missed out on hearing some very interesting
lines, including the following: "The white

00:03:11.469 --> 00:03:14.079
cold rose up, and the Walkers rose with it.

00:03:14.079 --> 00:03:19.170
And the sun hid its face for a lifetime, ashamed
at something none could discover".

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:24.050
In the cut scene, Gilly claims she knows what
made the sun do that and tells Sam that Craster

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:28.579
was drunk once when the time came to give
one of his baby boys away and he told the

00:03:28.579 --> 00:03:31.400
child, "Come on, time to meet your brothers".

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:35.219
Gilly also reveals that some of Craster's
older wives referred to the White Walkers

00:03:35.219 --> 00:03:37.010
as "Craster's Sons".

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:40.680
Gilly then thinks back to the time when a
White Walker attacked her, Sam and her baby

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.830
and questions whether he was one of her brothers.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:47.940
Now, I wonder whether this scene was cut because
the audience already knows about Craster's

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:51.439
sons being turned into White Walkers, which
we saw in season four.

00:03:51.439 --> 00:03:55.999
However, it's not clear whether any living
character on the show really knows this, though

00:03:55.999 --> 00:04:00.909
Jon Snow did catch a glimpse of one of Craster's
sons being taken in season 2.

00:04:00.909 --> 00:04:04.920
Maybe Gilly's reveal will be included next
season instead, especially if it makes a difference

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.480
to how the living can defeat the army of the
dead.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:11.099
But it's a shame that Gilly's lines were cut
this season as they would have made her role

00:04:11.099 --> 00:04:15.580
a bit more meaningful and they would also
have highlighted her part in uncovering important

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:20.220
information, even if by chance, like she did
in episode 5 with Rhaegar's annulment of his

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.620
marriage to Elia Martell.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:27.220
And while we're on the subject of scenes with
Sam, the first episode showed a humorous montage

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:31.250
of what life was like for the budding maester
after he arrived at the Citadel.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:34.910
And although it felt plenty long enough as
it was, there's actually an edit of the scene

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:39.620
which is seven to eight minutes long which
the episode director has described as "hilarious".

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:43.750
So, perhaps we'll see that as a Blu-ray extra?

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:48.950
We finally got to see Arya briefly reunite
with her long-lost direwolf Nymeria this season,

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:53.500
but our other favourite direwolf Ghost was
sadly chopped from his only scene which was

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:54.780
planned for episode two.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:58.490
According to the season 7 outline, there was
a short scene where Ghost saw Jon off from

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:00.530
Winterfell as he left for Dragonstone.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:05.220
In the cut scene, Jon told his direwolf, "Look
after anyone named Stark, boy!", which feels

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:09.740
like a touch of irony from the writers given
the full reveal of Jon's true heritage later

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.110
in the season.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:15.880
It's a shame Ghost was, erm, ghosted this
season, but the reason was probably financial.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.160
Game of Thrones' budget for special effects
will have already been stretched with the

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:23.310
need for a lot more dragon and White Walker
action, and, apparently, direwolves are more

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.910
expensive to animate than CGI dragons.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:30.699
I suspect also a decision was made that we
should see Nymeria instead as she hasn't been

00:05:30.699 --> 00:05:35.389
seen since Arya had to leave her in the woods
in season one, and their reunion underlined

00:05:35.389 --> 00:05:37.919
just how much has changed for each of them
since then.

00:05:37.919 --> 00:05:42.750
In fact, this is not the first time that Ghost
has had his screentime cut down as a scene

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:46.900
was deleted from season six where Ghost menaced
Alliser Thorne and other Night's Watchmen.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:50.980
And according to the director of Battle of
the Bastards, Ghost was going to have a big

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:55.620
part in that episode, but it was just too
expensive, and when they had to choose between

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:59.990
Wun-Wun and the direwolf, they picked the
mighty giant instead.

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:04.050
One character who brings some humour to most
scenes he's in is Bronn, so it was a shame

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:07.629
that the scene of him and Tyrion having a
little reunion that was originally intended

00:06:07.629 --> 00:06:10.389
to be in the fifth episode was dropped from
filming.

00:06:10.389 --> 00:06:14.080
It looks like it would have occurred just
before Jamie arrives at the secret meeting

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:17.330
with Tyrion that Bronn helped set up in King's
Landing.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:21.539
Of course, we did finally see the two men
back together on screen in the season finale,

00:06:21.539 --> 00:06:24.720
though given how much fun the scenes they
share together often are, it would have been

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:27.600
great to see more of them.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:31.430
Littlefinger's death was a long time coming
in Game of Thrones and it took seven seasons

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:35.560
of his scheming to finally come crashing down
on him before the Starks realised that he

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.539
was the one who'd set everything in motion.

00:06:38.539 --> 00:06:42.759
Sansa even admitted she was a slow learner
in the final episode after still getting played

00:06:42.759 --> 00:06:45.430
by Littlefinger throughout much of season
7.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:49.320
In fact, there's a deleted scene where Sansa
goes to Bran to ask him for his help before

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:51.810
she executes her own sister Arya.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:55.690
Actor Isaac Hempstead Wright, who plays Bran,
revealed in an interview with Variety that,

00:06:55.690 --> 00:07:00.740
"it suddenly occurred to Sansa that she had
a huge CCTV department at her discretion and

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:04.820
it might be a good idea to check with him
first before she guts her own sister.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:09.229
So, she goes to Bran, and Bran tells her everything
she needs to know."

00:07:09.229 --> 00:07:12.840
According to Hempstead Wright, they did actually
film this scene, but I can see a couple of

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:14.730
possibilities for why it got the chop.

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:18.560
On the one hand, if it had been included,
it would have taken away from the drama of

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:22.639
the scene where Sansa calls Arya in and it
looks like she's about to sentence Arya to

00:07:22.639 --> 00:07:25.660
death, but then she turns the tables on Littlefinger.

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:30.360
Also, the deleted scene further highlights
Sansa's ongoing naivety given the fact she

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:35.120
was still getting manipulated by Littlefinger
and ultimately needed Bran's help to figure

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:37.490
out what was really going on.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:42.560
The season finale set up numerous storylines
to propel us into Season 8, but there is one

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:47.840
crucial scene detailed in the episode outline
which didn't make it into the final episode.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:52.389
The cut scene would have occurred just after
Jaime stormed off from King's Landing in disgust

00:07:52.389 --> 00:07:56.879
following Cersei's refusal to honour her agreement
to send the Lannister army north against the

00:07:56.879 --> 00:07:58.000
Night King.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:01.629
The scene is set at the Red Keep in King's
Landing and has Cersei waking up suddenly

00:08:01.629 --> 00:08:04.770
in the middle of the night to discover her
bedclothes covered in blood.

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:09.259
This scene, which implies Cersei has just
miscarried, would have made a big difference

00:08:09.259 --> 00:08:13.600
to how season 7 ended, and it feels like it
would also have had strong parallels with

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:19.090
the scene we saw in the finale of Lyanna Stark
lying in a bloody bed having just given birth.

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:24.340
As season 7 left Cersei still apparently pregnant
though, her future baby has already given

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:26.500
rise to a number of fan theories.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:30.979
One such theory is that Tyrion has made a
deal with Cersei behind Dany's back to arrange

00:08:30.979 --> 00:08:34.849
for Cersei's new child to inherit the Iron
Throne after Daenerys.

00:08:34.849 --> 00:08:38.890
We know that Tyrion was concerned about the
succession and Dany's apparent inability to

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:43.890
have children, but what we don't know is if
he had to agree to something in order to change

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:47.089
Cersei's mind and make her publically support
Dany and Jon.

00:08:47.089 --> 00:08:51.200
And Tyrion didn't look very happy when Dany
and Jon were hooking up at the end of the

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:57.220
episode, likely because of the political problems
their romantic relationship could cause; but,

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:01.930
if that Cersei fan theory is correct, Tyrion
could also be worried that if Dany does conceive

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:04.970
her own child it would scupper his deal with
his sister.

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:09.371
In any case, I do wonder whether this cut
scene has been moved to season 8, meaning

00:09:09.371 --> 00:09:11.680
that we might still see Cersei miscarry.

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:17.110
Indeed, her miscarriage may be foreshadowed
in Jamie's words that, "Our child will never

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:18.950
be born if the dead come south".

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:23.720
Of course, Jaime was thinking of the Night
King's undead army, but technically the undead

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:28.160
have already come south in the form of the
wight that Jon and Dany brought to the Dragonpit.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:32.490
I think the way the wight clawed at Cersei
after it came dangerously close to her could

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:35.670
also be some ominous foreshadowing for Cersei
and her baby.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:40.000
For example, Cersei could die either through
miscarriage or in childbirth, which could

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:44.420
fulfil the valonqar prophecy that I talked
about in detail in my video predicting who

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:46.600
will die in Season 8.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:51.010
Alternately, it's possible that the showrunners
have decided to go the route of Cersei lying

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:55.230
about being pregnant, so the scene could have
been cut for that reason.

00:09:55.230 --> 00:10:00.010
So, what do you think about the season 7 deleted
scenes and do you think any of them should

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:01.510
